'''''Chenopodium strictum''''', the '''lateflowering goosefoot''', is a species of annual herb in the family [[Amaranthaceae]] (pigweed). It have a self-supporting growth form and simple, broad leaves. Individuals can grow to 55&nbsp;cm tall.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Chenopodium strictum Roth - Encyclopedia of Life|url=https://eol.org/pages/1283680|access-date=2022-02-04|website=eol.org}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Mifsud|first=Stephen|date=2002-08-23|title=Chenopodium strictum (Striated Fat Hen) : MaltaWildPlants.com - the online Flora of the Maltese Islands.|url=https://www.maltawildplants.com/AMAR/Chenopodium_strictum.php|access-date=2022-02-15|website=www.maltawildplants.com|language=en-us}}</ref>

